        <h2 class="mt-16 text-4xl font-black sm:text-5xl">History &amp; Significance of {attraction.fullName}</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-black/70">{attraction.fullName} began life as <strong>{attraction.legacyName}</strong>, the name still used by most locals and on Mussoorie Road signage. As the site grew into a full zoological park it was renamed <strong>{attraction.fullName}</strong>, and the Malsi name is now formally recorded as its former name in municipal references.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-black/70">Its significance lies in conservation rather than scale: ex-situ wildlife conservation, biodiversity conservation, environmental education and wildlife rescue are the stated objectives, making the park a reference point for how the Doon Valley combines tourism with conservation outreach.</p>
